@startuml Hexagonal Architecture - Execution Flow

!define FRAMEWORK_COLOR #E8F4FD
!define TEST_PROJECT_COLOR #FFF2CC
!define PROTOBUF_COLOR #F8CECC
!define EXTERNAL_COLOR #FFE6CC

title Hexagonal Architecture - Multi-Protocol Execution Flow

actor "REST Client" as RestClient EXTERNAL_COLOR
actor "RabbitMQ Producer" as RabbitProducer EXTERNAL_COLOR
actor "Direct Caller" as DirectCaller EXTERNAL_COLOR

package "Framework - Primary Adapters" FRAMEWORK_COLOR {
    participant "REST Controller\n(Auto-generated)" as RestController FRAMEWORK_COLOR
    participant "RabbitMQ Listener\n(Auto-generated)" as RabbitListener FRAMEWORK_COLOR
    participant "UseCaseExecutor" as Executor FRAMEWORK_COLOR
    participant "UseCaseRegistry" as Registry FRAMEWORK_COLOR
    participant "InputValidator" as Validator FRAMEWORK_COLOR
}

package "Test Project - Business Logic" TEST_PROJECT_COLOR {
    participant "CreateUserUseCase" as UseCase TEST_PROJECT_COLOR
}

package "Test Project - Secondary Adapters" TEST_PROJECT_COLOR {
    participant "InMemoryUserRepository" as Repository TEST_PROJECT_COLOR
    participant "RabbitMQEventPublisher" as EventPublisher TEST_PROJECT_COLOR
}

database "In-Memory Storage" as Storage EXTERNAL_COLOR
queue "Event Queue" as EventQueue EXTERNAL_COLOR

== REST Flow ==
RestClient -> RestController : POST /users\n{username, email}
RestController -> Executor : execute("create-user", request)
Executor -> Registry : getUseCase("create-user")
Registry --> Executor : CreateUserUseCase
Executor -> Validator : validate(request)
Validator --> Executor : ✓ valid
Executor -> UseCase : execute(CreateUserRequest)

UseCase -> Repository : existsByUsername(username)
Repository -> Storage : check username
Storage --> Repository : false
Repository --> UseCase : false

UseCase -> Repository : save(id, username, email)
Repository -> Storage : store user
Storage --> Repository : ✓ saved

UseCase -> EventPublisher : publishUserCreated(id, username, email)
EventPublisher -> EventQueue : publish event
EventQueue --> EventPublisher : ✓ published

UseCase --> Executor : CreateUserResponse
Executor --> RestController : CreateUserResponse
RestController --> RestClient : HTTP 200\n{id, statusMessage}

== RabbitMQ Flow ==
RabbitProducer -> RabbitListener : message on "user.create" queue\n{username, email}
RabbitListener -> Executor : execute("create-user", request)
note right : Same execution path as REST
Executor -> Registry : getUseCase("create-user")
Registry --> Executor : CreateUserUseCase
Executor -> Validator : validate(request)
Validator --> Executor : ✓ valid
Executor -> UseCase : execute(CreateUserRequest)

UseCase -> Repository : existsByUsername(username)
Repository --> UseCase : false
UseCase -> Repository : save(id, username, email)
UseCase -> EventPublisher : publishUserCreated(id, username, email)
UseCase --> Executor : CreateUserResponse
Executor --> RabbitListener : CreateUserResponse
RabbitListener --> RabbitProducer : ✓ processed

== Direct Call Flow (Testing) ==
DirectCaller -> UseCase : execute(CreateUserRequest)
note right : Direct call bypasses framework\nfor pure unit testing
UseCase -> Repository : existsByUsername(username)
Repository --> UseCase : false
UseCase -> Repository : save(id, username, email)
UseCase -> EventPublisher : publishUserCreated(id, username, email)
UseCase --> DirectCaller : CreateUserResponse

note over RestController, RabbitListener
**Key Insight:**
Same business logic (CreateUserUseCase)
executed identically across all protocols
end note

note over UseCase
**Business Logic:**
• Protocol agnostic
• Pure domain logic
• Easy to test
• Single source of truth
end note

note over Repository, EventPublisher
**Secondary Adapters:**
• Implement infrastructure concerns
• Swappable implementations
• Testable with mocks
end note

@enduml